## What happens (reproduced)
```js
const t0 = Date.now();
const timer = new Promise((r) => setTimeout(() => r(Date.now() - t0), 100));
const work = (async () => { execFileSync("sleep", ["2"]); })();
await Promise.all([timer, work]);   // the 100 ms timer fired at 2007 ms
```
On a slow disk, a chain of sync `git` or `df` calls can stall a monitoring run long enough that every OTHER probe "times out". The report then says everything is down.

## Fix
Use the async APIs (`execFile` with `util.promisify`, or `spawn`) anywhere other work runs concurrently. Keep `*Sync` for one-shot scripts.
